 ```
 
 
+## Symlinks
+
+`zip` and `squashfs` archives can contain symbolic links. These are
+skipped unless `-l`/`--links` is in use, when they are exposed as
+regular files whose name has the `.rclonelink` suffix and whose
+contents are the link target, just like the local backend. This means
+you can copy them to a destination which supports symlinks and they
+will be recreated.
+
+```
+$ rclone lsl --links :archive:/tmp/test.zip
+        5 2026-09-28 14:16:59.000000000 src/file.txt
+        8 2026-09-28 14:16:59.000000000 src/link.txt.rclonelink
+$ rclone copy --links :archive:/tmp/test.zip /tmp/out
+$ ls -l /tmp/out/src/link.txt
+lrwxrwxrwx 1 user user 8 Sep 28 14:16 /tmp/out/src/link.txt -> file.txt
+```
+
+A regular file in the archive whose name happens to end in
+`.rclonelink` is still exposed as a regular file.
+
 ## Modification times
 
 Modification times are preserved with an accuracy depending on the archive type.
